## For each teammate (and yourself), rate 1–5:

**Scale anchors:** 5 = consistently exceptional · 4 = consistently solid · 3 = adequate, some unevenness · 2 = a real problem the team has felt · 1 = effectively absent on this dimension

| # | Dimension | What you're rating |
|---|---|---|
| 1 | **Contribution & reliability** | Took a fair share of work and delivered it when promised. |
| 2 | **Quality of work** | Delivered work met the team's definition of done — reviewable, correct, documented. |
| 3 | **Collaboration & communication** | Responsive per the charter's norms; kept the team informed; made others' work easier. |
| 4 | **Initiative & ownership** | Found work rather than waiting; unblocked others; acted like a founder, not a passenger. |
| 5 | **Response to feedback** | Engaged review and disagreement professionally — neither defensive nor absent. |

**The charter check.** *Measured against our charter's definition of "pulling your weight," this person is:*
☐ Exceeding ☐ Meeting ☐ Below ☐ Well below

